    "statement": "Steady-state detect latency is 14.58 ms on the original vocabulary and 13.44 ms on the new one (-7.9%, within 10%), so detecting against a changed vocabulary is no dearer. The 16.2 ms the change itself cost is paid once, on the cold path. The change is not free on the frame path either: the *first* detect after it costs 122.85 ms, 108.26 ms more than a steady one, because ultralytics' `set_classes` drops the predictor and the next call rebuilds it. Re-warm the detector with one throwaway detect on the cold path and the frame path never sees it. The two vocabularies ran in alternating blocks and each arm is pooled over all of its detects, so a drifting clock lands on both; the block medians in order were 14.70, 13.17, 14.82, 13.82, 13.99, 13.38 ms.",
